#: includes/abilities/woocommerce-manage.php:4160
msgid "Published with no price, so WooCommerce renders no add-to-cart button. The product is in the catalogue and in search results, and cannot be bought."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/woocommerce-manage.php:4161
msgid "Set regular_price with nibwp/wc-update-product, or unpublish it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/woocommerce-manage.php:4170
msgid "Out of stock with backorders off, but still published. Every visitor who finds it is turned away at the product page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/woocommerce-manage.php:4171
msgid "Restock it with nibwp/wc-bulk-update-stock, allow backorders, or unpublish it until it is back."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/woocommerce-manage.php:4182
msgid "No product image. The shop and category pages show a placeholder, and a placeholder does not sell."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/woocommerce-manage.php:4183
msgid "Add an image with nibwp/wc-update-product."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/woocommerce-manage.php:4196
msgid "No product category beyond the store default, so it appears in no category listing and in no category-based menu or filter. Only search and a direct link will find it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/woocommerce-manage.php:4197
msgid "Assign a category with nibwp/wc-update-product — nibwp/wc-list-categories shows what exists."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/woocommerce-manage.php:4218
msgid "A variable product with no variations. The product page offers a choice that has nothing in it, so there is no way to add anything to the basket."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/woocommerce-manage.php:4219
msgid "Add variations with nibwp/wc-create-variation, or change the product type to simple."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/woocommerce-manage.php:4237
msgid "This variation has no price, so WooCommerce hides it from the selector without a word. Customers who want that combination cannot buy it and see no reason why."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/woocommerce-manage.php:4238
msgid "Set regular_price on it with nibwp/wc-update-variation, or delete the variation."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/woocommerce-manage.php:4255
msgid "No SKU, while the rest of the catalogue has them. Every export, product feed and stock take that keys on SKU quietly skips this product."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/woocommerce-manage.php:4256
msgid "Give it a SKU with nibwp/wc-update-product."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: coupon expiry date.
#: includes/abilities/woocommerce-manage.php:4293
#, php-format
msgid "Expired on %s but still published. Anyone who has the code from an old email or a voucher site types it, gets a refusal, and often abandons the basket rather than asking."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/woocommerce-manage.php:4296
msgid "Set it to draft with nibwp/wc-update-coupon, or extend date_expires if it should still work."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/woocommerce-manage.php:4308
msgid "Its usage limit is used up, but it is still published. The code is dead and anyone still holding it finds that out at checkout."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/woocommerce-manage.php:4309
msgid "Raise usage_limit or set the coupon to draft with nibwp/wc-update-coupon."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/woocommerce-manage.php:4320
msgid "Grants free shipping with no minimum spend, so a single cheap item ships for nothing and the postage comes out of the margin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/woocommerce-manage.php:4321
msgid "Set minimum_amount with nibwp/wc-update-coupon to the basket value that makes free shipping pay for itself."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: number of days, 2: order total.
#: includes/abilities/woocommerce-manage.php:4357
#, php-format
msgid "Paid and sitting in processing for %1$d days. %2$s was taken and nothing has shipped, which is how a chargeback starts."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/woocommerce-manage.php:4361
msgid "Fulfil it and move it to completed with nibwp/wc-update-order-status, or refund it with nibwp/wc-create-refund and tell the customer why."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: number of days.
#: includes/abilities/woocommerce-manage.php:4374
#, php-format
msgid "On hold for %d days. Either the payment never arrived and the order should be cancelled so the stock goes back, or it did arrive and the customer is still waiting."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/woocommerce-manage.php:4377
msgid "Chase the payment, or cancel it with nibwp/wc-update-order-status."
msgstr ""

