#: includes/integrations-page.php:577
msgid "Manage the Elementor header, footer and block templates on this site: list them, create one, set which pages and roles it appears on, and switch the builder's own widgets on or off. Also reports which templates are published with no display rules, so they render nowhere."
msgstr ""

#: includes/integrations-page.php:589
msgid "Manage this element pack's theme builder templates: list the headers and footers it stores, create one, and set the display rules that decide where it appears. Also switches any of the pack's elements and page extensions on or off, and reports templates that are published with no display rules, so they render nowhere."
msgstr ""

#: includes/integrations-page.php:601
msgid "Manage the templates and custom widgets this add-on stores: list the header and footer templates, create one, switch it on and set which pages it covers, and turn the add-on's own feature modules on or off. Also reports templates that were never opened in Elementor and ones published with nothing to show them on."
msgstr ""

#: includes/integrations-page.php:613
msgid "Manage the Happy Elementor Addons pack on this site: list the widgets it contributes to the editor and switch any of them on or off, and work with its theme builder templates — headers, footers, single and archive layouts — including the pages each one is shown on. Also reports templates that were never opened in Elementor, or that are published with no display rules and so appear nowhere."
msgstr ""

#: includes/integrations-page.php:625
msgid "Manage Premium Addons for Elementor on this site: report its version, list every widget it contributes to the Elementor registry, and switch any single one of its widgets, site-wide extensions or per-widget SVG-draw options on or off without disturbing the rest. Also reports which of them are currently off, which is usually the reason a section renders as nothing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/integrations-page.php:637
msgid "Manage this element pack on this site: list the headers, footers, archive and single layouts and popups it keeps in one template library, list its mega menu dropdowns and the widgets built with its widget builder, create a template, and switch any of its widgets or section extensions on or off. Also reports templates that were never opened in Elementor, so they output nothing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/integrations-page.php:649
msgid "Manage this element pack on this site: report its version, list the widgets it contributes to the Elementor editor, read one widget's full control schema, and find which pages are built with it. Switch any single one of its modules — the widgets and the site-wide extensions it lists together and stores together — on or off without disturbing the rest, and report which are off, the usual reason a section renders as nothing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/integrations-page.php:661
msgid "Manage the Jeg Kit pack on this site: list the elements it contributes to the editor and switch any of them on or off, and work with its header, footer and theme builder templates — list them, create one, and set which pages, archives or post types each one is shown on. Also reports templates that were never opened in Elementor, and published ones whose display rules were never stored, which output nowhere."
msgstr ""

#: includes/integrations-page.php:673
msgid "Manage this add-on pack on this site: list the widgets it contributes to the Elementor editor, read one widget's full control schema before building with it, find which pages are built with a given widget, and switch any of its widgets on or off. A widget switched off is never registered with Elementor at all, so a page already using it keeps the widget in its saved data and renders nothing in its place — the audit reports how many are off before anything is changed. This pack keeps no template post type of its own, so there are no template actions here."
msgstr ""

#: includes/integrations-page.php:685
#: includes/integrations-page.php:745
msgid "Manage this widget pack on this site: report its version, list every widget it contributes to the Elementor editor, read one widget's full control schema, find the pages built with it, and switch any single widget off or back on. It keeps no templates of its own, so this is inventory, usage and the widget on/off list rather than a template library."
msgstr ""

#: includes/integrations-page.php:697
msgid "Take stock of this widget pack on this site: list the widgets it contributes to the editor, read one widget's full control schema so a layout can be built with it, and find which pages and templates already use it. This is inventory and usage rather than management — the pack keeps its widget catalogue and each widget's on/off state in database tables of its own, so widgets are switched on and off from the add-on's own Elements screen, and its templates are saved as Elementor library posts that the Elementor abilities handle."
msgstr ""

#: includes/integrations-page.php:709
msgid "Manage this global template pack on this site: list the templates it keeps in one library, create one, set which post type or taxonomy a template takes over and whether it applies to all of them, and switch the pack's own modules on or off. Every template can also be inserted anywhere by shortcode, so the audit only reports the three kinds that really are matched by a stored rule."
msgstr ""

#: includes/integrations-page.php:721
msgid "Take stock of this widget pack on this site: list the widgets it contributes to the editor, read one widget's full control schema so a layout can be built with it, and find which pages and templates already use it, which is the question that matters before removing or replacing the pack. This is inventory and usage rather than management — the pack registers no templates of its own and has nothing an owner can switch on or off, so there is nothing else here to manage."
msgstr ""

#: includes/integrations-page.php:733
msgid "Manage this slider pack on this site: list the slides it keeps as its own post type, create one, retitle or delete it, list the widgets it contributes to the Elementor editor, read one widget's control schema, and find which pages are built with them. The pack keeps no display rules and no on/off switches, so where a slide appears is decided by the widget or the shortcode that collects it, and this integration says so rather than offering settings that do not exist."
msgstr ""

#: includes/integrations-page.php:757
msgid "Manage this element pack on this site: list the widgets it contributes to the editor and switch any of them on or off, and work with its theme builder templates — header, footer, single and blog layouts — including which template each slot is set to. Also reports templates that were never opened in Elementor, and published templates no slot is set to, so they appear nowhere."
msgstr ""

#: includes/integrations-page.php:769
msgid "Manage this widget pack on this site: report its version, list every widget it contributes to the Elementor editor, read one widget's full control schema, find the pages built with it, and switch any single widget off or back on. It keeps no template library of its own — its theme builder builds on Elementor's own saved templates — so this is inventory, usage and the widget on/off list rather than a template library."
msgstr ""

#: includes/integrations-page.php:781
msgid "Manage this widget pack on this site: report its version, list the widgets it contributes to the Elementor editor, read one widget's full control schema so a layout can be built with it, and find which pages already use it. Switch any single one of its widgets on or off without disturbing the rest, and report which are off — the usual reason a section renders as nothing. The pack keeps no templates of its own, so the layouts its widgets sit in are ordinary posts and pages that the Elementor abilities handle."
msgstr ""

#: includes/integrations-page.php:793
msgid "Manage this widget pack on this site: list the fifteen widgets it contributes to the Elementor editor, read one widget's full control schema so a layout can be built with it, find which pages already use it, and switch any of its elements on or off — the pack gates every widget registration on that switch, so one that is off is not in the editor at all. It keeps no templates of its own, so there is nothing else here to manage."
msgstr ""

#: includes/integrations-page.php:805
msgid "Manage the Rometheme kit on this site: its header, footer, archive, single, search and 404 templates, which pages each applies to, whether each is switched on, and which of the kit's modules are enabled. Also reports templates that are published but inactive, so they render nowhere."
msgstr ""

#: includes/integrations-page.php:817
msgid "Run the mailing list from where the work is: lists and who is on them, subscribers added, updated, unsubscribed or moved between lists, custom subscriber fields, newsletters and post-notification campaigns with their open and click statistics, and the sending method's own queue. Audits the three things that quietly kill a list — lists with nobody on them, campaigns stuck in the queue, and a bounced or never-confirmed share large enough to say the list is decaying. There is deliberately no action that sends a campaign to a list: irreversible mail to real people is not something to trigger from a tool call. A test send to one named address is available and says so. A subscriber's unsubscribe token or link hash never leaves, because holding one lets somebody act as that person."
msgstr ""

#: includes/integrations-page.php:829
msgid "Build and run forms without opening the builder: list them, read one with its whole field structure, create one from a description, add, update, reorder or remove fields, and set the success message, redirect, required fields and anti-spam. Reads entries, counts them over a period, and marks them read. Audits the two failures nobody notices until a customer complains — a form with no notification at all, and a form that has never received a single entry. The field structure is written in exactly the shape the plugin's own builder writes, so a form this touches still opens there. Entries are personal data and sit behind the plugin's own entries capability; captcha secrets and mail keys are reported as a name and whether they are set."
msgstr ""

#: includes/integrations-page.php:841
msgid "Manage forms and their entries: list forms, read one with its fields, create and rename, set the success message, redirect and email notifications, and read, count or delete entries. Audits forms with no notification configured and forms that never received an entry. Because these forms are built as Elementor content, the field structure lives in Elementor's saved data — so field writes are read-only here rather than risk a form that no longer opens in its editor, and the response says so plainly. A form id is checked against the plugin's own post type before any capability, so a delete cannot be handed the id of a page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/integrations-page.php:853
msgid "Build surveys and read what they found, in aggregate: surveys with their questions and answer options, per-question answer counts and percentages, response totals over a period, and an audit of surveys published but never answered or questions with no options to choose from. Answers are what a real person said, so the aggregate actions are the ones to reach for; the individual-response reads are bounded and never return a respondent's IP address or email — a logged-in respondent is reported as a flag, not an identity. Deleting a survey deletes every response anybody ever gave it, which that action says before it does it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/integrations-page.php:865
msgid "Run the licence desk for a store: search keys by status, product, order, customer or expiry, create them, change a status, expiry or activation limit, manage generators and what they are attached to, read and deactivate activations, and find a customer's licences by order or email. Audits the four things that cost support time — licences expiring soon, licences over their activation limit, keys never activated, and orders whose licences were never generated. A licence key is a bearer credential: a search or listing returns a masked form and the metadata, never the whole key. One deliberately named action reveals a single whole key, because an owner does legitimately need to resend one, and it says that it is handing over a live credential."
msgstr ""

#: includes/integrations-page.php:877
msgid "Build with the real block vocabulary instead of guessing at it: every block this version registers, each with its actual attribute schema read live from the block registry, so an agent writes attribute names that exist. Reports and changes which individual blocks are switched on or off, the global colours and typography, and which posts use a given block. Audits the commonest “my section disappeared” report — posts still holding a block that is currently switched off, which stays in the saved content and renders nothing. Posts are checked one at a time, so a listing can hold fewer than the site has and says how many it skipped."
msgstr ""

#: includes/integrations-page.php:889
msgid "Give an agent the block vocabulary it needs to build with: every block type this version registers with its real attribute schema read from the registry, which posts and pages are built with a given block, the plugin's global style and settings defaults, and its reusable styles. Audits posts whose block markup no longer validates and blocks left sitting on placeholder content. Anything touching a specific post asks about that post, not about posts in general, and a listing says how many it had to leave out."
msgstr ""

#: includes/integrations-page.php:901
msgid "Build with every block this version registers, each with its attribute schema read live from the block registry rather than from a list that goes stale. Reads and writes the global settings and theme styles, manages the template and section library with the rules that decide where each one shows, and finds which posts use a given block. Audits posts still holding a block this build no longer registers — they stay in the saved content and render nothing. An id from a caller is treated as a claim: the post type is checked first and alone, so a delete cannot be handed the id of an ordinary page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/integrations-page.php:913
msgid "Answer the one security question an owner cannot answer from the dashboard: is this site actually protected. Reports whether the firewall runs before WordPress loads or only after it, when the last scan ran and how it ended, what it found and how much of it is critical, which installed plugins or themes are known to be vulnerable, whether administrators are still allowed to sign in with a password alone, and what has been blocked lately as counts by reason. Read-mostly on purpose: three writes and no others — start a scan, block an IP, unblock an IP. Nothing here can switch the firewall or the scanner off, change or whitelist a rule, turn off two-factor, or repair or delete a file the scanner flagged; those stay in wp-admin where the consequences are in front of a person. The plugin's API key and any two-factor secret are never returned, and the blocked-traffic report gives counts rather than visitors' addresses."
msgstr ""

#: includes/integrations-page.php:925
msgid "Answer the question a silently broken store cannot: can this site send mail at all. Reports the active mailer and whether it is fully configured, the From name and address, the recorded send failure, and the errors logged over a period — then runs a connection test that drives the provider session without delivering anything. Also checks SPF, DKIM and DMARC. Credentials are never returned: every API key, password, client secret and token is reported by name and whether it is set, and a value that comes from wp-config.php is named as a constant rather than read out."
msgstr ""

#: includes/integrations-page.php:937
msgid "Manage member accounts and what they can reach: who is pending, approved, rejected or deactivated, and move them between those states; the plugin's own roles and permissions; its registration and profile forms and their fields; member directories; content restriction, site-wide and per post; and the emails it sends. Member reads are asked per member, so a response can hold fewer records than the site has and says how many it skipped. A password hash, a session token, an application password or a capability map never leaves, whatever it is stored under."
msgstr ""

#: includes/integrations-page.php:949
msgid "Manage cloaked affiliate links: list them, create one, repoint a destination, rename a slug, set the redirect type and the nofollow, new-window and uncloak flags, and organise link categories. Finds which posts use a given link, and reports the three things that quietly lose clicks — links with no destination at all, cloaked paths that shadow a real page, and destinations that now answer with a redirect or an error. Renaming a slug or changing the link prefix breaks copies already published elsewhere, so those actions ask for confirmation and say what they will break."
msgstr ""

#: includes/integrations-page.php:961
